# eth_dma_mc AXI4 master formal proof (SymbiYosys).
#
# Proves the AXI4 VALID/READY discipline of `eth_dma_axi_engine` — the single
# AXI4 master port of the multi-channel scatter-gather DMA `eth_dma_mc`
# (S15 §3; eth-axi-v0.md §2 rules 1-2, §7 props 1-2):
#   F1  no VALID withdrawal before the handshake, with stable AW/AR payload
#       (AWADDR/AWLEN/AWID, ARADDR/ARLEN/ARID);
#   F2  W held stable while stalled (WDATA/WSTRB/WLAST freeze until WREADY);
#   F3  WLAST asserted exactly on the last beat of the burst and only there;
#   F4  no lost / duplicated beats: one beat is counted per accepted W beat, the
#       write stream leaves E_W exactly at that last beat, R beats are accepted
#       only while the read burst is open and it closes exactly on RLAST, and
#       the FSM transition relation makes a second AW (or AR, or completion)
#       per grant unreachable;
#   F5  single outstanding transaction (tx_ready_o only in E_IDLE, and an
#       accepted request always enters an address phase);
#   F6  BREADY only after the write data stream finished (E_W -> E_B -> E_IDLE).
#
# The properties are written as inductive relations over (state, inputs, next
# state) plus one-cycle VALID-stability checks on registered outputs, so the
# proof holds by k-induction at UNBOUNDED depth — there is no harness length
# bound and no property-only counting state.  Environment assumptions are the
# AXI/DRAM-socket contracts: a producer holds a presented W beat until accepted,
# and a compliant slave ends a burst with RLAST on the last requested beat (an
# erroring read may end early — eth-axi-v0.md §9.4).
#
# The cover task witnesses completed read and write bursts, including erroring
# ones, so the safety proof is non-vacuous.  Liveness/progress (fairness of
# READY) is out of scope.
#
# Run:  sby -f eth_dma_mc.sby     (picked up by `make formal`)
[tasks]
prove
cover

[options]
prove: mode prove
prove: depth 24
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 24

[engines]
prove: smtbmc
cover: smtbmc

[script]
read -formal eth_dma_axi_engine.sv
prep -top eth_dma_axi_engine

[files]
ethereal-shell/rtl/dma/eth_dma_axi_engine.sv
